{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>ולערב יחלק שלל</b> in gematria equals the sacrifices. The initial letters of the words after their names, such as בכורי אחיך אתה לחוף חמור ידין גדוד שמנה אילה בן זאב עולה, sum to שם\"ה, equal to the count of the solar days. And the final letters of the blessings, such as עלה בישראל מחלב צידון עובד יהיה עקב מלך שפר אחיו שלל עולה, sum to שנ\"ד, equal to the count of the lunar days. And this is what is stated: \"Thus said YHWH, who gives the sun for light by day, the laws of the moon and stars for light by night, etc. — if these laws could depart from before Me, said YHWH, then the seed of Israel would cease from being a nation before Me for all days.\" Jacob placed Dan before Gad according to the order of their birth; Moses placed Gad before Dan because he is buried in his portion."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The Ba'al HaTurim reads the initial and final letters of the blessing-word sequences (including tribe names as delimiters) as gematria totals for solar and lunar cycles. The values שמ\"ה = 345 and שנ\"ד = 354 correspond to the solar and lunar year day-counts. The unaddressed prophetic quotation is from Jeremiah 31:34-35."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:52.164860296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}